# Flexi Block ACF Builder

- Define one `FieldsBuilder` per flexi block and always include a human-readable `label`.
- Organize fields into `Content`, `Design`, and `Layout` tabs when applicable.
- Include full heading-tag choices: `h1` to `h6`, `span`, and `p`.
- Prefer `addWysiwyg()` over textarea fields for rich copy; pair frontend output with a `.wp_editor` wrapper.
- Use single ACF link arrays for CTAs and links; never split URL, title, and target into separate fields.
- Use descriptive field names, clear instructions, sensible defaults, and conditional logic where it improves editor UX.
- Add the shared `padding_settings` repeater for block spacing using `xxs`, `xs`, `mob`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `xxl`, and `ultrawide`.
- Keep image fields compatible with WordPress media metadata so frontend templates can derive meaningful alt and title fallbacks.
- Match the naming and tab structure style already used in existing block builders such as `acf_what_we_offer.php`.
- Keep field groups concise, reusable, and aligned with existing flexi block conventions.
